.TH SDE-PANEL 1 "October 2026" "SDE 0.1 Alpha" "Selviana Desktop Environment"
.SH NAME
sde-panel \- taskbar, application menu, quick settings, tray and clock
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sde-panel
[\-\-menu | \-\-quick\-settings | \-\-calendar | \-\-version]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBsde-panel\fR shows the panel at the bottom or top of the screen: application menu with search, pinned applications, the list of open windows, the system tray (XEmbed and StatusNotifierItem/AppIndicator), quick settings for network, sound, brightness, battery and Do Not Disturb, and a clock with a calendar.
.PP
Right-click an application in the menu or on the taskbar to pin it; drag pinned icons to reorder them. The panel can hide itself automatically (see \fBsde-settings\fR(1)).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-menu
Open or close the application menu of the running panel (bound to the Super key).
.TP
.B \-\-quick\-settings
Open or close quick settings (Super+A).
.TP
.B \-\-calendar
Open or close the calendar (Super+C).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/sde/sde.conf
System-wide default settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sde/sde.conf
Per-user settings, written by \fBsde-settings\fR(1).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/sde/session.log
Messages of the current session (the previous one is kept as \fIsession.log.old\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sde-session (1),
.BR sde-panel (1),
.BR sde-desktop (1),
.BR sde-notifyd (1),
.BR sde-settings (1)
